{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_u4bv6tlfg4kisuwhajoaoobdoiuz3m5jtf3bnymbfcqo4pj2t7oa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Full surface enumeration\nThe C library is a single translation unit (`c_src/src/lib.c` + `c_src/include/lib.h`). Built it two ways (raw `gcc -shared` and via its own `CMakeLists.txt`); `nm -D` on both shows exactly one export:\n\n```\nT crc16\n```\n\nThe `tflac_crc16_tables[8][256]` array is `static const` in the header, so it is **not** exported (no namespace/rename macros exist in the header either).\n\n## What I wrote (in the current dir, `c_src/` untouched)\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `panic = \"abort\"` so no unwinding escapes across FFI.\n- **`src/tables.rs`** — all 8×256 = 2048 table values transcribed verbatim from the header (the table is *not* the textbook slice-by-8 derivation of row 0, so it had to be copied literally rather than computed).\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn crc16(*const u8, u32, u16) -> u16`, plus `tflac_u8/u16/u32` aliases. Preserves the C semantics exactly: the slice-by-8 body, the `crc16 << 8` truncation to 16 bits in the tail loop (`wrapping_shl`), the `(crc >> 8) ^ *d++` index, and the fact that the pointer is never dereferenced when `len == 0`. Internals use a safe slice + safe indexing; the only `unsafe` is the single `from_raw_parts`.\n\n## Verification (my own commands, not a sub-agent report)\n1. `cargo build --release` — clean, zero warnings.\n2. **Symbol diff is empty**: `diff` of the sorted `nm -D --defined-only` name lists for the C `.so` and `libtranslated_rust.so` → identical (`crc16` only).\n3. **Table equality**: re-parsed both `c_src/include/lib.h` and `src/tables.rs` → all 8 rows / 2048 values match exactly.\n4. **Differential ABI test**: a `dlopen`-based harness loading both `.so`s side by side and comparing return values over **265,075** cases — `NULL`/zero-length, all 256 single-byte values × 8 seeds, every length 0–64 with random data over 4000 iterations, random buffers up to 512 bytes, and all-`0x00`/all-`0xFF` patterns for every length 0–512. Result: **PASS, 0 failures**, against both the `gcc` and the CMake builds of the C library."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_read_input_tokens":40555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1269,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ff51d15-d729-4f7f-a568-57619775e241","uuid":"63c0bee0-9dc1-4b23-833e-07f430399674","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:08:58.262Z"}
